<title>USA: TABLE - Bank of Nova Scotia sells notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bank of Nova Scotia sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Bank of Nova Scotia was priced Monday, according to joint-lead manager UBS Securities Inc.</p>
<p>Scotia McLeod was the other manager on the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER BANK OF NOVA SCOTIA</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	 COUPON 6.50 PCT   MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.875  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.529 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD +40/5-YR   CALLABLE NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: If the notes are not called in five-years they become quarterly floating rate notes paying at a spread of 100 basis points over 3-month LIBOR.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
